 "notes": "Plan of the collier Sagona, 'Le Grec' (53.3 x 8.6 m), broken in two by a mine: the stern and midships section stands upright on shelly sand at 47 m (propeller 47 m, poop 40 m, holds 38-40 m, coursives 35-37 m) and the 15 m bow section lies 60-80 m to the north, parallel to the port side, with the foremast beside it. Position from Wikipedia; dimensions, depths and layout from nicoblon.free.fr (after Joncheray and Brunner) and frenchdiver-wim-csr. No heading is published: bow east is assumed because it puts the bow piece both north and off the port side, as the sources say. The Donator lies about 430 m WSW. Positions along the hull are approximate.",
